..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4737: 4.1.13.1 Hardware Interrupt Request Register
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4738:             The read-only hardware interrupt request register (HIRR) indicates all
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4739:             outstanding interrupt requests and summary bits at the time it is read. Each
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4740:             bit in the HIRR corresponds to a bit that must be set in the hardware interrupt
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4741:             enable register (HIER, Section 4.1.13.4) to enable an interrupt request. When
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4742:             it is read, the HIRR also returns the state of software and AST interrupt
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4743:             requests.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4744: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4745:                                                                  Note
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4746: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4747:                   When read, the HIRR can return a value of zero if the hardware
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4748:                   interrupt was released before the read (passive release).
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4749: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4750:             All interrupt requests are blocked while executing in PALmode. (For more
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4751:             information about interrupt operations, see Section 2.2.3.)
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4752: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4753:             Figure 4?9 shows the HIRR format, and Table 4?14 describes its fields.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4754: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4755: 4.1.13.2 Software Interrupt Request Register
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4756:             The read and write software interrupt request register (SIRR) controls software
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4757:             interrupt requests. Each bit in the SIRR corresponds to a bit that must be set
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4758:             in the software interrupt enable register (SIER, Section 4.1.13.5) to enable an
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4759:             interrupt request. When it is read, the SIRR also returns the state of hardware
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4760:             and AST interrupt requests.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4761: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4762:             All interrupt requests are blocked while executing in PALmode. (For more
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4763:             information about interrupt operations, see Section 2.2.3.)
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4764: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4765:             Figure 4?9 shows the SIRR read format, and Table 4?14 describes its fields.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4766:             Figure 4?11 shows the SIRR write format, and Table 4?17 describes its fields.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4767: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4768: Figure 4?11 SIRR Write Format
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4769: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4770: 63       48 47                 33 32       0
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4771: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4772:     IGN         SIRR                  IGN
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4773:                 <15:1>
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4774: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4775:                                       Internal Processor Registers 4?23
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4776: Table 4?17 SIRR Write-Format Field Description
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4777: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4778: Bits Field Type Description
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4779: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4780: 63:48  IGN RW                      Ignored when written.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4781: 47:33
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4782:        SIRR RW                     Software interrupt request--These bits correspond to
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4783:        <15:1>                      software interrupt enable 15 through 1 in the SIER
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4784:                                    (Section 4.1.13.5). Writing a one to any of these bits
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4785: 32:0 IGN RW                        when the corresponding enable bit is set, requests the
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4786:                                    corresponding interrupt. Writing a zero to any of these bits
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4787:                                    clears the corresponding interrupt request.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4788: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4789:                                    Ignored when written.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4790: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4791: 4.1.13.3 Asynchronous Trap Interrupt Request Register
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4792:             The read and write asynchronous trap interrupt request register (ASTRR)
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4793:             contains AST interrupt request bits for each processor mode. To generate an
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4794:             AST interrupt, the following must occur:
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4795: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4796:             ? The corresponding enable bit must be set in the asynchronous trap enable
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4797:                   register (ASTER, Section 4.1.13.6).
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4798: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4799:             ? The processor must be in the selected processor mode or a higher privileged
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4800:                   mode according to the current value of current mode (CM) bits in the
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4801:                   processor status register (PS, Section 4.1.15).
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4802: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4803:             In addition, to enable AST interrupt requests, bit SIER2 must be set in the
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4804:             software interrupt enable register (SIER, Section 4.1.13.5). This provides a
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4805:             mechanism to lock out AST requests over certain interrupt priority levels
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4806:             (IPLs).
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4807: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4808:             When it is read, the ASTRR also returns the state of software and hardware
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4809:             interrupt requests.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4810: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4811:             All interrupt requests are blocked while executing in PALmode. (For more
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4812:             information about interrupt operations, see Section 2.2.3.)
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4813: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4814:             Figure 4?9 shows the ASTRR read format, and Table 4?14 describes its fields.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4815:             Figure 4?12 shows the ASTRR write format, and Table 4?18 describes its
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4816:             fields.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4817: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4818: 4?24 Internal Processor Registers
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4819: Figure 4?12 ASTRR Write Format
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4820: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4821: 63  52 51 50 49 48 47                            0
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4822: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4823:     USEK
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4824: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4825:     IGN A A A A                 IGN
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4826: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4827:     RRRR
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4828: 
