..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4830: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4831: Bits Field Type Description
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4832: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4833: 63:52 IGN RW           Ignored when written.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4834: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4835: 51  UAR RW             User mode AST request--This bit corresponds to user mode
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4836:                        AST interrupt enable. Writing a one to this bit when the
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4837: 50  SAR RW             corresponding enable bit is set, requests the interrupt.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4838:                        Writing a zero to this bit clears the interrupt.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4839: 49  EAR RW
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4840:                        Supervisor mode AST request--This bit corresponds to
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4841: 48  KAR RW             supervisor mode AST interrupt enable. Writing a one
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4842:                        to this bit when the corresponding enable bit is set,
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4843: 47:0 IGN RW            requests the interrupt. Writing a zero to this bit clears
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4844:                        the interrupt.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4845: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4846:                        Executive mode AST request--This bit corresponds to
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4847:                        executive mode AST interrupt enable. Writing a one to this
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4848:                        bit when the corresponding enable bit is set, requests the
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4849:                        interrupt. Writing a zero to this bit clears the interrupt.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4850: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4851:                        Kernel mode AST request--This bit corresponds to kernel
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4852:                        mode AST interrupt enable. Writing a one to this bit when
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4853:                        the corresponding enable bit is set, requests the interrupt.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4854:                        Writing a zero to this bit clears the interrupt.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4855: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4856:                        Ignored when written.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4857: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4858: 4.1.13.4 Hardware Interrupt Enable Register
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4859:             The read and write hardware interrupt enable register (HIER) enables the
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4860:             hardware interrupt requests described in Table 4?19. There is a one-to-one
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4861:             correspondence between the interrupt request and enable bits. When set, a
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4862:             bit in this register enables the corresponding interrupt request in the HIRR
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4863:             (Section 4.1.13.1); otherwise, the request is disabled.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4864: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4865:             When read, the HIER returns all the interrupt enables described in Table 4?15.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4866: 
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4867:                                 Internal Processor Registers 4?25
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4868: Figure 4?10 shows the HIER read format, and Table 4?15 describes its fields.
..\_scratchpad\21066_66a_hrm.txt:4869: Figure 4?13 shows the HIER write format, and Table 4?19 describes its fields.

