web search: "21066" "Interrupt Vector and Special Cycle Register"
codex
LCA does connect its installed handler to the default ISA bus, so this is reachable wiring. I also found a completion gap: Alpha’s CPU callbacks set and clear `irq_asserted`, but I have not yet found code that consumes it. The manual line numbers at `175` and `510` point to the contents table; I’ve located the body sections.
